  "notes": [
    "Datasets are the existing synthetic experiment cohorts (read only; MANIFEST hashes verified before and after).",
    "Historical outcomes come from the harness's oracle reviewer (ground-truth corrections), not humans.",
    "Similarity weights were fixed before evaluation (no tuning); seeds 4-6 are a held-out repetition.",
    "Synthetic errors are injected at random with respect to clinical features, so little predictive signal from similarity is expected; the random-neighbour baseline is reported alongside.",
    "Retrieval recall@K is not reported: no ground-truth similarity set exists.",
    "Recommendation agreement with the ground-truth correction op is near-tautological on this data: each synthetic error type has one canonical correction op in the generator, and the oracle history applied exactly those ops. It shows the recommendation cites the recorded action correctly, not clinical insight."
